        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): keep diagnostics error message truncation UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`formatCodexErrorForDisplay()` in `extensions/codex/src/command-handlers.ts` uses `formatCodexTextForDisplay(error).slice(0, 500)` to truncate error messages for display. When the 500-char boundary lands in a surrogate pair, the output contains an orphan high surrogate.\n\n**Proof on main:**\n```js\nconst input = \"x\".repeat(499) + \"🚀\";         // length 501\ninput.slice(0, 500)[499] === \"\\ud83d\"           // → true, orphan high surrogate\n```\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n1. Exported `formatCodexErrorForDisplay` for direct testing\n2. Replaced `.slice(0, 500)` with `truncateUtf16Safe(text, 500)`\n3. Added 2 test cases including surrogate-pair boundary proof\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Codex diagnostics error messages keep emoji intact at the 500-char boundary\n- No behavior change for ASCII text\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Boundary test: 499 chars + emoji → verified no broken surrogate in formatted output\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
